dd a few  drops of food coloring and stir again  then at the glitter and continue  stirring in a separate cup add the hot  water and borax and stir until it's all  combined the two mixtures into One Bowl  and your frozen silly putty is ready to  go  glow-in-the-dark playdough to make this  all-natural glow-in-the-dark Play Doh  fresh too  so the b-fifty complex vitamins until  they turn into a powder then mix the  powder with 2 cups of flour 4 teaspoons  of cream of tartar and 2/3 cup of salt  when everything is combined add 2 cups  of warm water and 2 tablespoons of  vegetable oil to the mixture put  everything together until it's smooth  add the solution to a saucepan and cook  it on medium heat until the potato forms  into a ball allow it to tool for a few  minutes take it into a dark room turn on  a backlight and watch it glow liquid  plastic get ready to completely wow your  friends because we're going to show you  how you can make this DIY liquid plastic  all on your own  slowly warm up a half cup of heavy cream  or milk when it begins to simmer clear  in a few spoonfuls of vinegar continue  adding spoonfuls of vinegar and preserve  slowly until the mixture begins to gel  let it cool for a bit and then wash the  gel mixture with water to clean it off  and you'll be left of liquid classes  that will keep you and your friends  entertained for hours for me jelly worms  these squirmy jelly worms are easy to  make and they taste delicious too you'll  need a pack raspberry jello an extra  pack of unflavored gelatin for extra  firmness 3/4 cups of whipping cream 3  cups of water blue coloring flexible  straws and 1 tall container to hold two  straws combine the gelatin in a bowl and  add the hot water let the mixture cool  until it's lukewarm then add the  whipping cream and food coloring gather  your straws and put them in the  container so they fit tightly add the  gelatin mixture inside each draw and let  it sit until they become firm then  squeeze the worms out of the straws and  proceed to devour them homemade gas  homemade GAC is made using four ounces  of Elmer's glue a quarter cup of hot  water and food coloring of your choice  and a half teaspoon of borax  pour the glue into a small container and  add half of the hot water mix together  with a spoon and then add the food  coloring dissolve the four acts with the  remaining hot water and stir then for  the borax and water into the glue  mixture and stir until it becomes solid  within minutes you'll have your very own  homemade gak water beads  making water beads is so easy and  they're edible to cook some tapioca  pearls on your stove for five minutes  using a little bit of water drain the  pearls from the water and rinse them  under cold water for a few  add a few drops of food coloring the  Brighton amount and let the coloring  absorb into the pearls for five minutes  then rinse the beads under cold water  after they dry you and your friends can  have fun playing with and eating your  edible water views slime  who doesn't love it we do a slime well  now you can make DIY slime using this  quick and simple recipe combine one cup  of water with one cup of cornstarch and  mix them together with your fingers  until it becomes confining add a few  drops of food coloring like a bright  green or blue and that's all it takes to  make DIY slime edible slime if you want  to kick things up a notch with your  slime you can make this edible version  for you and your friends to play with  and snack on at the same time just take  a quarter cup of basil seeds and add a  16 ounce box of corn starch mix the two  together with your hands and then add  food coloring and two and a half cups of  water stir well and knead the mixture  like bread dough for about five minutes  the basil seeds will begin to absorb the  water and the mixture will thicken once  the slime feels nice and smooth it's  ready to be played with and eaten will  you be making any of these DIY projects  to impress your friends react in the  comment section down below and don't  forget to give this video a big thumbs  up  [Music]

